1005 {\cf20 //}\par
1006 {\cf20 // Finding the right font...}\par
1007 {\cf20 //}\par
1008 {\cf20 // You should really just solve this offline, keep your own tables}\par
1009 {\cf20 // of what font is what, and don't try to get it out of the .ttf file.}\par
1010 {\cf20 // That's because getting it out of the .ttf file is really hard, because}\par
1011 {\cf20 // the names in the file can appear in many possible encodings, in many}\par
1012 {\cf20 // possible languages, and e.g. if you need a case-insensitive comparison,}\par
1013 {\cf20 // the details of that depend on the encoding & language in a complex way}\par
1014 {\cf20 // (actually underspecified in truetype, but also gigantic).}\par
1015 {\cf20 //}\par
1016 {\cf20 // But you can use the provided functions in two possible ways:}\par
1017 {\cf20 //     stbtt_FindMatchingFont() will use *case-sensitive* comparisons on}\par
1018 {\cf20 //             unicode-encoded names to try to find the font you want;}\par
1019 {\cf20 //             you can run this before calling stbtt_InitFont()}\par
1020 {\cf20 //}\par
1021 {\cf20 //     stbtt_GetFontNameString() lets you get any of the various strings}\par
1022 {\cf20 //             from the file yourself and do your own comparisons on them.}\par
1023 {\cf20 //             You have to have called stbtt_InitFont() first.}\par
1024 \par
1025 \par
